  "id": "inner-directed",
  "term": "inner-directed",
  "definition": "Inner-directed refers to a style of social orientation in which a person is guided mainly by internalized principles and values rather than by tradition or immediate peer approval. In the source, this logic is linked to intergenerational cultural transmission as a basis for judging and pursuing social honor.",
